#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using Qiskit to implement ideas from the multiple-systems lesson."
msgstr ""
"Używanie Qiskit do implementacji zagadnień z lekcji o układach "
"wieloqubitowych."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation"
msgstr "Implementacja w Qiskit"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/multiple-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""
"<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-"
"information/multiple-systems/qiskit-implementation.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we took a first look at the `Statevector` and `Operator` classes in Qiskit, and used them to simulate operations and measurements on single qubits.\n"
"In this section, we'll use these classes to explore the behavior of multiple qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"W poprzedniej lekcji zapoznałeś się po raz pierwszy z klasami `Statevector` i `Operator` w Qiskit i użyłeś ich do symulowania operacji oraz pomiarów na pojedynczych qubitach.\n"
"W tej sekcji użyjemy tych klas, żeby zbadać zachowanie wielu qubitów.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start by importing the `Statevector` and `Operator` classes, as well as the square root function from `NumPy`.\n"
"Hereafter, generally speaking, we'll take care of all of our required imports first within each lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Zaczniemy od zaimportowania klas `Statevector` i `Operator` oraz funkcji pierwiastka kwadratowego z `NumPy`.\n"
"Od tej pory, co do zasady, będziemy dbać o to, żeby wszystkie wymagane importy znajdowały się na początku każdej lekcji.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tensor products {#tensor-products}"
msgstr "Iloczyny tensorowe {#tensor-products}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Statevector` class has a `tensor` method, which returns the tensor product of that `Statevector` with another, given as an argument.\n"
"The argument is interpreted as the tensor factor on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Klasa `Statevector` ma metodę `tensor`, która zwraca iloczyn tensorowy danego `Statevector` z innym, podanym jako argument.\n"
"Argument jest interpretowany jako czynnik tensorowy po prawej stronie.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, below we create two state vectors representing $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ and use the `tensor` method to create a new vector, $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Notice here that we're using the `from_label` method to define the states $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ rather than defining them ourselves.\n"
msgstr ""
"Na przykład poniżej tworzymy dwa wektory stanu reprezentujące $\\vert 0\\rangle$ i $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ i używamy metody `tensor`, żeby utworzyć nowy wektor $\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Zauważ, że używamy tutaj metody `from_label` do zdefiniowania stanów $\\vert 0\\rangle$ i $\\vert 1\\rangle,$ zamiast definiować je ręcznie.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ |01\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$ |01\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Other allowed labels include \"+\" and \"-\" for the plus and minus states, "
"as well as \"r\" and \"l\" (short for \"right\" and \"left\") for the "
"states\n"
msgstr ""
"Inne dozwolone etykiety to „+\" i „-\" dla stanów plus i minus, a także „r\""
" i „l\" (skróty od „right\" i „left\") dla stanów\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert {+i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n"
"\\vert {-i} \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, \"+\", \"-\" or \"right\" and \"left\" come from the context of "
"quantum mechanical spin, in which a component of spin may point to the left "
"or the right in an experiment; it is not referring to the right-most or "
"left-most qubit in systems of multiple qubits. Here's an example of the "
"tensor product of $\\vert {+} \\rangle$ and $\\vert {-i} \\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutaj „+\", „-\" lub „right\" i „left\" pochodzą z kontekstu "
"kwantowomechanicznego spinu, w którym składowa spinu może wskazywać w lewo "
"lub w prawo w doświadczeniu; nie chodzi tu o skrajnie prawy lub skrajnie "
"lewy qubit w układach wieloqubitowych. Oto przykład iloczynu tensorowego "
"$\\vert {+} \\rangle$ i $\\vert {-i} \\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\\frac{1}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |01\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2} "
"|10\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\\frac{1}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |01\\rangle+\\frac{1}{2} "
"|10\\rangle- \\frac{i}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative is to use the `^` operation for tensor products, which "
"naturally gives the same results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternatywą jest użycie operatora `^` do iloczynów tensorowych, który "
"naturalnie daje te same wyniki.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Operator` class also has a `tensor` method (as well as a `from_label` "
"method), as we see in the following examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Klasa `Operator` ma również metodę `tensor` (a także metodę `from_label`), "
"co widać w poniższych przykładach.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}  \\\\\n"
" 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 & - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0  \\\\\n"
" \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Again, like in the vector case, the `^` operation is equivalent.\n"
msgstr "Podobnie jak w przypadku wektorów, operator `^` jest równoważny.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compound states can be evolved using compound operations as we would expect — just like we saw for single systems in the previous lesson.\n"
"For example, the following code computes the state $(H\\otimes I)\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ for $\\vert\\phi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert {-i}\\rangle$ (which was already defined above).\n"
msgstr ""
"Złożone stany można ewoluować za pomocą złożonych operacji dokładnie tak, jak można by się spodziewać — podobnie jak widzieliśmy dla pojedynczych układów w poprzedniej lekcji.\n"
"Na przykład poniższy kod oblicza stan $(H\\otimes I)\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ dla $\\vert\\phi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert {-i}\\rangle$ (który został już zdefiniowany powyżej).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2} |01\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle- \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{2} |01\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is some code that defines a $CX$ operation and calculates $CX "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ for $\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes "
"\\vert 0 \\rangle.$ To be clear, this is a $CX$ operation for which the "
"left-hand qubit is the control and the right-hand qubit is the target. The "
"result is the Bell state $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Oto kod, który definiuje operację $CX$ i oblicza $CX \\vert\\psi\\rangle$ "
"dla $\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle.$ "
"Żeby było jasne, jest to operacja $CX$, w której qubit po lewej stronie jest"
" qubitem kontrolnym, a qubit po prawej stronie jest qubitem docelowym. "
"Wynikiem jest stan Bella $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |00\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |11\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Pomiary cząstkowe {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we used the `measure` method to simulate a measurement of a quantum state vector.\n"
"This method returns two items: the simulated measurement result, and the new `Statevector` given this measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"W poprzedniej lekcji użyliśmy metody `measure` do symulowania pomiaru wektora stanu kwantowego.\n"
"Metoda ta zwraca dwie rzeczy: symulowany wynik pomiaru oraz nowy `Statevector` po tym pomiarze.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default, `measure` measures all qubits in the state vector.\n"
"We can, alternatively, provide a list of integers as an argument, which causes only those qubit indices to be measured.\n"
"To demonstrate this, the code below creates the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Domyślnie `measure` mierzy wszystkie qubity w wektorze stanu.\n"
"Możemy alternatywnie podać listę liczb całkowitych jako argument, co powoduje, że mierzone są tylko qubity o tych indeksach.\n"
"Żeby to zademonstrować, poniższy kod tworzy stan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert w\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert 001\\rangle + \\vert 010\\rangle + \\vert 100\\rangle}{\\sqrt{3}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert w\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert 001\\rangle + \\vert 010\\rangle + \\vert 100\\rangle}{\\sqrt{3}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and measures qubit number 0, which is the rightmost qubit.\n"
"(Qiskit numbers qubits starting from 0, from right to left. We'll return to this numbering convention in the next lesson.)\n"
msgstr ""
"i mierzy qubit numer 0, czyli qubit skrajnie prawy.\n"
"(Qiskit numeruje qubity począwszy od 0, od prawej do lewej. Wrócimy do tej konwencji numerowania w następnej lekcji.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |001\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} "
"|010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |001\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} "
"|010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} |100\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |010\\rangle+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} |100\\rangle$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ |100\\rangle$$\n"
msgstr "$$ |100\\rangle$$\n"
